WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.219
Permissive licenses: Apache 2.

2
00:00:02.499 --> 00:00:03.843
0 and MIT.

3
00:00:04.123 --> 00:00:11.312
Many open models now ship under the same licenses as ordinary software, and those are the easiest to work with.

4
00:00:11.592 --> 00:00:12.637
Apache 2.

5
00:00:12.917 --> 00:00:21.493
0 grants a perpetual, worldwide, royalty-free right to use, copy, modify, sublicense, and distribute the work (section 2).

6
00:00:21.773 --> 00:00:30.755
It also grants an explicit patent license from each contributor, which ends for anyone who sues claiming the work infringes a patent (section 3).

7
00:00:31.035 --> 00:00:43.941
Its conditions are about notices: when you redistribute, include the license, mark files you changed, keep the copyright and attribution notices, and carry forward the contents of any NOTICE file (section 4).

8
00:00:44.221 --> 00:00:50.920
It grants no trademark rights (section 6), so you can ship a fine-tune but not call it by the publisher’s brand.

9
00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:58.709
At the time of writing, OpenAI’s gpt-oss models, Google’s Gemma 4, Ai2’s Olmo models, Qwen3.

10
00:00:58.989 --> 00:01:06.840
8-27B, and several Mistral models (including Mistral Small 4 and Mistral Large 3) use Apache 2.

11
00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:07.888
0.

12
00:01:08.168 --> 00:01:09.448
MIT is shorter.

13
00:01:09.728 --> 00:01:18.944
It permits essentially anything, including selling, on the single condition that you keep the copyright and permission notice, and it disclaims all warranties.

14
00:01:19.224 --> 00:01:20.504
Unlike Apache 2.

15
00:01:20.784 --> 00:01:24.027
0, its text contains no explicit patent grant.

16
00:01:24.307 --> 00:01:33.629
DeepSeek’s recent model cards state that both the repository and the weights are MIT licensed, and Microsoft’s Phi models use MIT.

17
00:01:33.909 --> 00:01:40.352
One caution that applies to both: the license on the weights says nothing about the outputs or the training data.

18
00:01:40.632 --> 00:01:48.483
A permissively licensed model can still produce text that infringes someone’s rights, and it can be trained on data with its own terms.

19
00:01:48.763 --> 00:01:55.824
License review covers what you may do with the artifact; your product still needs its own checks on what the model says.
